# OTLP trace export is opt-in by endpoint. Boot gates the exporter on the presence of
# management.opentelemetry.tracing.export.otlp.endpoint, and that key cannot be conditionally
# omitted from YAML, so the mapping from OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_ENDPOINT (a base URL; /v1/traces is
# added unless it is already there) and OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_TRACES_ENDPOINT (used as written)
# happens here instead. It is a listener, not an environment post-processor, so that it runs after
# Boot's own mapping of the same variables, which always adds /v1/traces and would double a full URL.
org.springframework.context.ApplicationListener=\
  com.dvarahq.gateway.autoconfigure.TracingExporterEnvironmentPostProcessor

# explains the boot failure when spring-jdbc stands the gateway.yaml store down and a
# consumer of one of its repositories then cannot be built.
org.springframework.boot.diagnostics.FailureAnalyzer=\
  com.dvarahq.autoconfigure.config.yaml.repo.YamlStoreStoodDownFailureAnalyzer
